Pin the TimePicker samples' clock.

WHY: upstream seeds all four samples with `LocalTime.now()`, so each render carries the wall clock
and the bytes change on the minute. The visual-diff bot then flags them on pull requests that do
not touch this module — measured on yschimke/wear-m3-catalog#449, where three renders at ONE commit
gave two hashes splitting on a minute boundary:

    16:55:54Z  bd75b44745fdfac6300bff72a15c7008
    16:56:08Z  bbdc6ba2d1aab162cde0242e550129ff
    16:56:18Z  bbdc6ba2d1aab162cde0242e550129ff

PINNED TO `:catalog`'s OWN INSTANT (00:00), not an arbitrary one. `sections/Pickers.kt` already
pins its picker stickers there for this exact reason, and the compare page puts a sample beside its
kit sticker — an instant is only worth pinning to the one the other side already pins to.

A renderer limitation rather than an upstream bug: `LocalTime.now()` is right for a sample someone
runs on a watch, and wrong for one captured as a still.

